-- title:
--   Frobenius-kernel coordinates of a connected p-divisible group over mathbb Fₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $h_0$ a natural number, and let $H$ be a family of commutative rings $H(v)$, $v\in\mathbb N$, each carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb Z/p$ whose comultiplication is cocommutative and which is finite as a $\mathbb Z/p$-module. Assume given bialgebra maps $s_v\colon H(v+1)\to H(v)$ that are surjective, that $\dim_{\mathbb Z/p}H(v)=p^{v h_0}$ for all $v$, and that $\ker s_v$ is the torsion ideal of $H(v+1)$ at $p^v$, i.e. the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon)$ under the algebra endomorphism obtained as the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity; assume also that each $H(v)$ is a local ring. Let $n\le w$, and let $d$ be the $\mathbb Z/p$-dimension of the cotangent module $I_1/I_1^2$ of the augmentation ideal $I_1$ of $H(1)$. Let $x\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,d\to H(w)$ take values in the augmentation ideal $I_w$ of $H(w)$ and be such that the classes of the $x_i$ span $I_w/I_w^2$ over $\mathbb Z/p$. Write $J$ for the ideal of $H(w)$ generated by $\{a^{p^n}: a\in I_w\}$. Then the $\mathbb Z/p$-algebra map $(\mathbb Z/p)[X_i : i\in \mathrm{Fin}\,d]\to H(w)/J$ sending $X_i\mapsto x_i$ (the evaluation $X_i\mapsto x_i$ followed by the quotient map) is surjective, and its kernel is exactly the ideal generated by the $X_i^{p^n}$.
--
--   This is the statement that the coordinate ring of the $n$-th Frobenius kernel of a connected $p$-divisible group of dimension $d$ over $\mathbb F_p$ is $\mathbb F_p[X_1,\dots,X_d]/(X_1^{p^n},\dots,X_d^{p^n})$, in the strong form that any lift of any spanning set of the cotangent space at the origin serves as a system of coordinates, so that compatible lifts along the tower give compatible presentations. It rests on the dimension count [`PDivisibleGroup.finrank_quotient_span_pow_augIdeal_eq_pow_of_isLocalRing`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.finrank_quotient_span_pow_augIdeal_eq_pow_of_isLocalRing) and feeds the construction of coordinates on the special fibre and of a surjection from a power series ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_ker_aeval_quotient_span_pow_augIdeal_eq_span_X_pow_of_isLocalRing.lean

